 .. note:: Usually items are monitored in total. If you want to expand the items (to prevent problems with different alignment etc.) then consider using the method |IDataItemListExpanding.CreateAndAddExpanding| instead.

 :return: An error code representing the result of the operation. In case of success, ERR_OK will be returned]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pstSymbol</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>GetItem</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the item at the given index.
 :return: The item at the index or 0 in case of an invalid index.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemBase</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>udiIndex</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequest</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequestHandling</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>ReleaseRequest</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>request</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequest</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomResponse</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequestCallback</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>RequestFinished</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when the execution of the given request is finished.

 .. note:: The method will be called no matter whether the request was executed successfully or not. Callees can find out about this fact by evaluating the according result.
 ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>request</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequest</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>response</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomResponse</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICredentials</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICredentialsProvider</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>GetCredentials</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Must return ERR_OK if called after a successfull |ICredentialsProvider.IsGetCredentialsFinished|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>uxiRequestId</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>credentials</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICredentials</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>IsGetCredentialsFinished</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Will return ERR_OK if the request is finished, ERR_PENDING if it is not yet 
 finished, ERR_DS_RETRYLOGIN if the login should be tried again, another error code in case of an error]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>uxiRequestId</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>LoginFailed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Will be called when a login failed due to wrong credentials
 The behaviour of the datasource afterwards depends on the return value. In case of 
 ERR_PENDING, the logincycle will be started again with a call to GetCredentials.
 In all other cases the driver will go to it's error state.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>uxiRequestId</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>tRetryWaitTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>LoginSucceeded</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Will be called when after a successful login.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>uxiRequestId</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>StartGetCredentials</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Will return an id of the question for credentials. This id can be used in 
 the following calls to |ICredentialsProvider.IsGetCredentialsFinished|]]></Comment><ReturnType>ULINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pstDataSource</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>udiErrorCode</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasource</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getCustomRequestHandling</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequestHandling</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>EnqueueCustomRequest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Enqueues the given request for sending to the connected device the next time this is possible.

 .. note:: It is possible to call this method without holding locks on the datasources (like |IDatasourcesMgr.BeginDataConfiguration|)

 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors| representing the result of the operation.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>request</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequest</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>finishedCallback</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICustomRequestCallback</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetCredentialsProvider</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Assigns the given credentials provider object to a specific datasource.
 :return: An error code representing the result of the operation]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>provider</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICredentialsProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesMgr</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>ActionRecordDelete</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesActionRecord</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ActionRecordingGetResult</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesActionRecord</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ActionRecordingStart</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>ActionRecordReplay</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>record</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesActionRecord</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>AllItemsOk</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will return ERR_OK when all active items of all datasources have the quality good
 else it will return ERR_DS_BADITEMS.
 It might return ERR_DS_MULTITASKING_LOCKED when it is currently not possible to have access to
 all datasources. In this case the client should call this method again later.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>BeginDataConfiguration</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method locks the concurrent task for monitoring items and allows subsequent accesses 
 to the configuration of the active. To unlock again afterwards, call |IDatasourcesMgr.EndDataConfiguration|

 .. important:: Before calling methods like |IDatasourcesMgr.UseData| or |IDatasourcesMgr.ReleaseData| it is necessary to do this syncronisation to prevent undefined behaviour.

 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>xBlocking</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>CreateItemList</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Creates a new item list that can be used for reading/writing synchronously for example.

 .. important:: Please remark that you have to release the returned object when it is no longer in use by calling |IDatasourcesMgr.DeleteItemList|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemList</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>udiInitialCapacity</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>DeleteItemList</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Deletes an item list and the items managed therin that was previously created using |IDatasourcesMgr.CreateItemList|
 :return: An error code representing the result of the operation. In case of success, ERR_OK will be returned]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>itemsList</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemList</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>EndDataConfiguration</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Releases a previously taken lock by |IDatasourcesMgr.BeginDataConfiguration| 
 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>GetDatasource</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the datasource representing the given object's name. 
 :return: The datasource object or 0 in case there is none with the given name.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasource</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>GetItemInfo</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemBase</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pstSymbol</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReadItemsSync</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Reads the given list of items synchronously. 

 .. important:: Please remark that the operation might take quite some time in case many items are contained within the list. For this time, the call is blocking!]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>items</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemList</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReleaseData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Deactivates the item of the given instance path from monitoring.

 .. note:: The items are reference counted so each call to |IDatasourcesMgr.UseData| or |IDatasourcesMgr3.UseDataExpanding| requires a matching call to ReleaseData

 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pstSymbol</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SetCredentialsProvider</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Assigns the given credentials provider object to all datasources.
 :return: An error code representing the result of the operation]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>provider</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ICredentialsProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>UseData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Activates the item of the given instance path for monitoring.

 .. note:: The items are reference counted so each call to |IDatasourcesMgr.UseData| requires a matching call to |IDatasourcesMgr.ReleaseData|

 .. note:: Usually items are monitored in total. If you want to expand the items (to prevent problems with different alignment etc.) then consider using the method |IDatasourcesMgr3.UseDataExpanding| instead.

 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pstSymbol</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>WriteItemsSync</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Writes the given list of items synchronously. 

 .. important:: Please remark that the operation might take quite some time in case many items are contained within the list. For this time, the call is blocking!]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>items</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemList</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemNameType</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NormalString</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ The name represents a POINTER TO a zero terminated STRING of the according length. Take care when derefercing using IEC operators! ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>strict</Name></Property><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Name><BitSize>128</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nameType</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemNameType</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nameData</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">INotificationClient</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>ListOperationDone</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when an operation on a list of variables was executed (eg. |IDatasourcesMgr.ReadItemsSync| or |IDatasourcesMgr.WriteItemsSync|) ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>xWriting</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ListOperationStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when an operation on a list of variables will be executed (eg. |IDatasourcesMgr.ReadItemsSync| or |IDatasourcesMgr.WriteItemsSync|) ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>xWriting</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ListValueRead</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a variable was read as part of a list operation (see |INotificationClient.ListOperationStart| or |INotificationClient.ListOperationDone|)]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>remoteName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pReadValue</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueType</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IBaseLibrary">TypeClass</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueSize</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ListValueWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a variable will be written as part of a list operation (see |INotificationClient.ListOperationStart| or |INotificationClient.ListOperationDone|)

 .. note:: 
		Please remark that this method will be called before the write operation is sent to the connected device. 
		For being sure about a successful execution the followup call of |INotificationClient.ListOperationDone| should be checked.  ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>remoteName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pWriteValue</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueType</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IBaseLibrary">TypeClass</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueSize</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReadRequestDone</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a read operation on one or more variables was executed. ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReadRequestStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a read operation on one or more variables will be executed. ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SingleValueRead</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a variable was read from the connected device]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>remoteName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pReadValue</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueType</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IBaseLibrary">TypeClass</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueSize</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SingleValueWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a variable will be written to the connected device

 .. note:: 
		Please remark that this method will be called before the write operation is sent to the connected device. 
		For being sure about a successful execution the followup call of |INotificationClient.WriteRequestDone| should be checked.  ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>remoteName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pOldValue</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pNewValue</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueType</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IBaseLibrary">TypeClass</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>valueSize</Name><Type>ULINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>WriteRequestDone</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a write operation on one or more variables was executed. ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>WriteRequestStart</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method will be called when a write operation on one or more variables will be executed. ]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>datasourceName</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">ItemName</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">PersistantItemListUsage</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>Unspecified</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>Recipes</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ The variable list is used for reading or writing recipes. Therefore it is expected that
 the usage details reflect the name of the recipe definition and that all variables of the recipe definition are added
 to the according list.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>strict</Name></Property><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemListPersistant</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemList</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getUsage</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">PersistantItemListUsage</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getUsageDetails</Name><ReturnType>WSTRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>1296</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>FinishedAdding</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method must be called by users of such a list once the insertion of items (using |IDAtaItemList.CreateAndAdd|)
 is finished. Afterwards the list can be registered within the affected datasource(s). After calling this method it
 is no longer possible to add additional items.
 :return: An error code representing the result of this operation.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesMgr2</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesMgr</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__getPersistantItemListCount</Name><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>AddNotificationClient</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method can be used to register an implementation of |INotificationClient| that will be notified about
 operations of the datasources.
 
 .. note:: Please remark that the number of notification clients might be limited so at least if registering several clients the return value should be evaluated.

 .. note:: The registered object can be removed using |IDatasourcesMgr2.RemoveNotificationClient| 

 :return: An error code that signals whether the registration was successful.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>client</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">INotificationClient</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>CreatePersistantItemList</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Creates an item list that will be registered automatically within the affected datasources
 after (re)connections of these datasources. An according list can be used in followup calls to
 |IDatasourcesMgr.ReadItemsSync| or |IDatasourcesMgr.WriteItemsSync|

 .. important:: Having such lists might slow down the connection 
 			   setup because the list has to be registered within the connected device!
  
 .. important:: Using this method and the related ones working on the list requires according locking around using |IDatasourcesMgr2.Lock| and |IDatasourcesMgr2.Unlock|
 
 .. note:: It is not supported to register several lists for the same usecase. 
 
 .. note:: Once the list is no longer necessary, it can be deleted using
			  |IDatasourcesMgr2.DeletePersistantItemList|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemListPersistant</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>usage</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">PersistantItemListUsage</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>usageDetails</Name><Type>WSTRING(80)</Type><BitSize>1296</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>udiInitialCapacity</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>result</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>DeletePersistantItemList</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Deletes a formerly created |IDataItemListPersistant|
  
 .. important:: Using this method and the related ones working on the list requires according locking around using |IDatasourcesMgr2.Lock| and |IDatasourcesMgr2.Unlock|
]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>itemsList</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemListPersistant</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>GetPersistantItemList</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the nth |IDataItemListPersistant| managed by the current instance. Can be used
 for iterating over all lists.
  
 .. important:: Using this method and the related ones working on the list requires according locking around using |IDatasourcesMgr2.Lock| and |IDatasourcesMgr2.Unlock|
]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemListPersistant</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>listNr</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Lock</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method locks the concurrent task for monitoring items and allows subsequent accesses to methods of
 the current instance. To unlock again afterwards, call |IDatasourcesMgr2.Unlock|

 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>xBlocking</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>RemoveNotificationClient</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method can be called to remove an object that was formerly registered using |IDatasourcesMgr2.AddNotificationClient|
 :return: An error code that signals whether the removal was successful.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>client</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">INotificationClient</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Unlock</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Releases a previously taken lock by |IDatasourcesMgr2.Lock| 
 :return: Returns a runtime system error code (see CmpErrors.library) or one of |Errors|]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Recipe_Management.SysTypes">RTS_IEC_RESULT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition2</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition</ExtendsType><Method><Name>GetRecipeVariableCount</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the number of recipe variables in the current recipe]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>GetRecipeVariableName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the name of the recipe variable from the corresponding recipe at the given index.
 The variable name will be returned as a pointer to the zero terminated characters in STRING encoding. 
 
 .. note:: For performance reasons this function assumes that CurrentlySelectedRecipe is assigned!]]></Comment><ReturnType PointerTo="1">BYTE</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>64</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>iVarIndex</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>errorCode</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelectionWithCompare</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>Compare</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition3</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition2</ExtendsType><Method><Name>GetRecipeValuesSizeOf</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Returns the recipe values from the corresponding recipe.
Possible last error values:
ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET, ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND, ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND, ERR_FAILED, ERR_OK 
]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pStrings</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The strings where the recipe values should be stored ]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><ArrayInfo PointerTo="1"><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>1</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSize</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of the string array. ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStartIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start index. Can be used for a scroll function (See example)]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSizeOfString</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of one string in the pStrings array ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Recipe_Management">RecipeManCommands</Name><BitSize>256</BitSize><SubItem><Name>_RecipeManager</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeManager</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_RecipeDefinition</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_bRecipeManagerSet</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>SetRecipeManager</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Sets the recipe manager the function block works with
 
Possible last error values:
ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET, ERR_OK

This method must not be called by the default user because it is set 
implicit in the function prvCheckRecipeManager which is called from all 
methods of the public interface.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeManager</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeManager</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name><Value>visu_coredev</Value></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>GetLastError</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the last error of the previous operation

 :return: See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>DeleteRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes a recipe from the recipe definition

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK| 

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>ResetLastInfo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Resets the last information

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>ReadAndSaveRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Reads the current PLC values into the recipe and afterwards stores the recipe into the standard recipe file

 The content of an existing file will be overridden.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_SAVE_ERR|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>GetRecipeVariableNames</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the recipe variable names from the corresponding recipe

 **Example:**

 We have 50 recipe variable names. We want to create a table which shows 10 recipe variable names at the same time.
 We define a string array ``strArr: ARRAY[0..9] OF STRING;``
 Corresponding to the ``iStartIndex`` we can get the recipe variable names from a specific area.

 	- ``StartIndex`` := 0; The variable names 0..9 are returned.
 	- ``iStartIndex`` := 20; The variable names 20..29 are returned.

 In this example:

 	- ``iSize`` := 10;
 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe definition. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pStrings</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The strings where the recipe values should be stored ]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><ArrayInfo PointerTo="1"><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>1</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSize</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of the string array. ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStartIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start index. Can be used for a scrolling function (See example)]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReadRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Reads the current PLC values into the recipe

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|
		- DataServer Errors from 16#2000 to 16#20FF, 
		- DataSourceDriver Errors from 16#2100 to 16#21FF

 DataServer and DataSourceDriver errors can occur if a DataServer and DataSource is configured beneth your current application (CODESYS HMI) and the command
 is called from the visualization.

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>LoadAndWriteRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Loads a recipe from the standard recipe file and afterwards writes the recipe into the PLC variables

 .. note::
    Entries in the recipe that do not include value assignments are not loaded and written. 
    Refer to the "Load and write Recipe" command.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_FILE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_MISMATCH|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_ALL_VARIABLES_WERE_LOADED|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>SaveRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Stores the recipe into the standard recipe file

 The content of an existing file will be overridden.
 The standard recipe file name is ``<recipe>.<recipedefinition>.<recipeextension>``.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_SAVE_ERR|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>CreateRecipeNoSave</Name><Comment><![CDATA[  Creates a new recipe in the specified recipe definition and afterwared reads the current PLC values into the new recipe

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_ALREADY_EXIST|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOMEMORY|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ResetLastError</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Resets the last error

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>WriteRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Writes the recipe into the PLC variables

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>GetRecipeValues</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the recipe values from the corresponding recipe.

 **Example:**

 We have 50 recipe values. We want to create a table which shows 10 recipe values at the same time.
 We define a string array ``strArr: ARRAY[0..9] OF STRING;``
 Corresponding to the ``iStartIndex`` we can get the recipe values from a specific area.

 	- ``iStartIndex`` := 0; The values 0..9 are returned.
 	- ``iStartIndex`` := 20; The values 20..29 are returned.

 In this example:

 	- ``iStringLength`` := 80; The default STRING has 80 characters.
 	- ``iSize`` := 10;
 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe definition. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pStrings</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The strings where the recipe values should be stored. ]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><ArrayInfo PointerTo="1"><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>1</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSize</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of the string array. ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStartIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start index. Can be used for a scrolling function. (See example). ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStringLength</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Length of a string in the pStrings array. It should correspond to the actual amount of characters. ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>GetRecipeNames</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the recipe names from the corresponding recipe definition

 **Example:**

 We have 50 recipes. We want to create a table which shows 10 recipe names at the same time.
 We define a string array ``strArr: ARRAY[0..9] OF STRING``;

 Corresponding to the ``iStartIndex`` we can get the recipe names from a specific area.

 	- ``StartIndex`` := 0; The names 0..9 are returned.
 	- ``iStartIndex`` := 20; The names 20..29 are returned.

 In this example:

 	- ``iSize`` := 10;
 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pStrings</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The strings were the recipe values should be stored ]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><ArrayInfo PointerTo="1"><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>1</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSize</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of the string array ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStartIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start index. Can be used for a scrolling function (see example)]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>LoadRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Loads a recipe from the standard recipe file

 The standard recipe file name is ``<recipe>.<recipedefinition>.<recipeextension>``.

 .. note::
    Entries in the recipe that do not include value assignments are not loaded and written. 
    Refer to the "Load and write Recipe" command.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_FILE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_MISMATCH|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_ALL_VARIABLES_WERE_LOADED|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>LoadFromAndWriteRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Loads a recipe from the specified recipe file and afterwards writes the recipe into the PLC variables


 .. note::
    Entries in the recipe that do not include value assignments are not loaded and written. 
    Refer to the "Load and write Recipe" command.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_FILE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_MISMATCH|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_ALL_VARIABLES_WERE_LOADED|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.

]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe definition. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>FileName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the file ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>recipeDefinition</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pPersistentRecipeHelper</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management" PointerTo="1">IPersistentRecipeHelper</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>recSel</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeSelection</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>RegisterDatasourceRecipeDefinition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Helper method that can be used to preregister variable lists for a recipe definition within devices connected via datasources.
 The intention of this function is to speedup reading/writing of recipes at the cost of an initial registration process
 after each connection setup of the affected datasources. If a recipe is read or written several times then this initial effort 
 is necessary only once and each read or write operation is executed faster.
 
 .. important:: 
 	This functionality does not automatically update the created variable list in case of online changes (eg. affecting the recipe definition). 
 	Therefore if online changes modify a recipe definition or locations of variables within a recipe definition, the
 	according list has to be setup again! This can be done by searching and deleting it using the methodes of |IDatasources.IDatasourcesMgr2|
 
 .. important:: 
 	This function might block until it is possible to access the datasources.

 .. note:: 
 	If there is no performance flaw when reading/writing recipe definitions over datasources then it's not necessary to call this method. 
 
 .. note:: 
 	The error code |CmpErrors.Errors.ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED| signals that one of the affected datasources does not support 
 	this feature and so it cannot be used at all.
 	The error code |IDatasources.Errors.ERR_DS_READONLY_ITEM| signals that at least one of the variables of the recipe definition is reaonly
 	and therefore the feature of preregistering according variable lists is not supported.
 
 :return: An error code representing the result of this operation.
 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe definition. ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>datasourcesMgr</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The global instance of the datasources manager. Typically pass g_Datasources ]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesMgr</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>recDef</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>dsMgr2</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDatasourcesMgr2</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>itemsList</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management.IDatasources">IDataItemListPersistant</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>recDef2</Name><Type Namespace="Recipe_Management">IRecipeDefinition2</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>varsCount</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pVarName</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>SetRecipeValues</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Sets the recipe values of the corresponding recipe

 **Example:**

 We have 50 recipe values. We want to create a table which sets 10 recipe values at the same time.
 We define a string array ``strArr: ARRAY[0..9] OF STRING;``
 Corresponding to the ``iStartIndex`` we can set the recipe values from a specific area.

 	- ``StartIndex`` := 0; The values 0..9 are set.
 	- ``iStartIndex`` := 20; The values 20..29 are set.

 In this example:
 	- ``iSize`` := 10;
 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

 See :ref:`ReturnValues` for a description of all possible errors.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DWORD</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>RecipeDefinitionName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	Name of the recipe definition ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeName</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Name of the recipe ]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pStrings</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The strings with the recipe values ]]></Comment><Type>STRING(80)</Type><ArrayInfo PointerTo="1"><LBound>0</LBound><Elements>1</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iSize</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Size of the string array. ]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iStartIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start index. Can be used for a scrolling function (see example)]]></Comment><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ReadAndSaveAs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Reads the current PLC values and stores the values in a recipe file without changing any existing recipe

 The content of an existing file will be overridden.

 :return: Possible last error values:

		- |ERR_RECIPE_DEFINITION_NOT_FOUND|
		- |ERR_RECIPE_SAVE_ERR|
		- |ERR_NO_RECIPE_MANAGER_SET|
		- |ERR_OK|

